## 4️⃣ Kerberos Authentication

Kerberos is a secure network authentication protocol that uses secret-key cryptography to authenticate users over an insecure network.

### 🔹 Key Components

- Key Distribution Center (KDC)
  - Authentication Server (AS)
  - Ticket Granting Service (TGS)

### 🔹 Kerberos Process

1. User requests Ticket Granting Ticket (TGT)  
2. KDC verifies and issues TGT + session key  
3. User requests service ticket  
4. KDC issues service ticket  
5. User accesses service  

✔ Prevents replay attacks  
✔ Uses time-stamped tickets  
✔ Commonly used in Active Directory environments  

